+Disabling retries
+~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
+
+Pass ``enabled=False`` to call a function exactly once, without retry policies,
+callbacks, or sleeps. Any exception propagates unchanged. This is useful during
+development and testing, and works with synchronous and asynchronous functions.
+
+.. code-block:: python
+
+    @retry(enabled=False)
+    def fetch_data():
+        return load_data()
+
+You can also pass ``enabled=False`` to ``Retrying`` or ``AsyncRetrying`` when
+calling a function directly, or use ``fetch_data.retry_with(enabled=False)()``
+to disable retries for a particular call. Retries are enabled by default.
+
 Retrying code block
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 
